            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"Ood5dTvPNoqnHMxOOrHlbFmOgxf\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\" old-record-id-MV6ddR5BNoaypkxjivHlXk9ngob\">Looking first at the ground floor, the entrance in the lower right corner of the traditional layout opens into a hallway along the right side of the building, with a bathroom and a kitchen on the left, both with their own separate spaces and doors. <strong>At the other end and along the shorter side</strong> is a traditional Japanese bedroom with a sliding door and a small cupboard, fitted with a kind of straw mat flooring called tatami. <strong>In the modern layout</strong>, the corresponding bedroom <strong>is</strong> <strong>reoriented along the longer side</strong> of the house and replaces the kitchen. Meanwhile, the original bathroom has been replaced by an open kitchen space, and the remaining space on this floor serves as a common living and dining area.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 19784,
